 "poem": "This Thursday, you left away\nYour soul to wake from sleepless day,\nThe rest of us, all for ours me\nToo dull a year and too deep solitary.\nI thought of you as you had away,\nAnd said the great words today\nAs if they were not past in years away:\n'Our souls are weary when anyway;\nBut let the world's wrongings sleep no today,\nOr let our souls be purged hereafter.' They\nSmiled back: I took my lips and smote separate\nMy clenched hands that clung meditate",
